    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0818" n="748" xml:id="pg748"/>

                <head>Mr. Corwin to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 20, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatches Nos, 43, 44, and 45, with the two treaties between the United
                    States and Mexico lately ratified at Washington. The ratifications will be
                    exchanged to-morrow, and the next day Mr. Plumb, with Captain Shufeldt, will
                    leave for Vera Cruz.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS CORWIN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of the United States, Washington,
                            D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
